      {
        "id": 115532,
        "name": "Unsafe_Bet",
        "username": "Unsafe_Bet",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/53a042/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-21T00:59:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Katsue\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/48/2012_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Katsue:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Against many of those Villains I would play it first turn. The Vengeful 5 I would definitely play it first turn, because they start off with so much nasty stuff that would be a pain to leave on the table.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But more nasty stuff will arrive fast, so you might be better off saving EoD for after, say, Revenant and the Hippo and Zhu Long and Everyman's Strength and Subtle Diversion are all in play.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Against Miss Information, you have a consequence free way of killing the first Distraction.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If the first-turn play was a Clue, your consequence is that you're waiting a lot longer before the killing of Miss Info can begin.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Against The Dreamer you are skipping the whole first half of the game, which can be very dangerous indeed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>But nowhere near as dangerous as the second half, which you probably shouldn't rush.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It's definitely a first turn play against Gloomweaver, since you can't use it to kill his Relics, so you may as well use it to kill his Zombies.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Killing 2-HP zombies is hardly worthy of EoD.&nbsp; Save it for when the nastier Cultists appear.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:43.596Z",
