      {
        "id": 115533,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-21T14:29:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>On End of Days first turn.</p><p>Most villains can get to a point on their first turn that End of Days can be very useful. Plague Rat, Spite, and The Ennead&nbsp;are about the only ones that do not. It's very heavy on what the villain's set-up is, what they play, and what kind the hero's have avaliable. It also is dependant on people's individual preferences.</p><p>An example being that La Capitan's set-up isn't End of Days worthy, but if she plays a Raiding Party of her first turn, then I am&nbsp; very likely to play End of Days.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
